   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project Outcome</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened national and subnational public sector management</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator 1</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">By the end of 2016:
(i) Civil service training institute functioning efficiently with 50% of staff and budget, and implementing a well-formulated annual training plan
(2011 baseline: civil service training institute established) 
Achievement: 50 
Progress/Status: (2018) PARTI now has 21 staff, of which 7 are female (36%).  PARTI estimates that it requires 50 staff to function fully, however, given the Government&apos;s budget constraints, staff number has increased slowly in the past 5 years (by about 1 or 2 staff per year).  PARTI is currently finalising its development strategy and curriculum framework based on Civil Servant Law 2016, the Training and Development Decree 2017 and MOHA Vision 2030 and 10-Year Strategic Plan (2016-2025). 
Data Source: Governance and Public Administration Reform Program secretariat progress reports on the use of the District Development Fund


MOHA annual report</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="0" year="2011"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2016-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2016-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="50"></target>
     <actual value="50"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator 3</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">(iii) Increased direct budget support from MOF received by 70 districts
(2011 baseline: 35 districts are receiving block grants through the District Development Fund) 
Achievement: 0 
Progress/Status: (2018) The number of civil servants trained under Component 2 Output 1 on PBFM, General Management and Gender Mainstreaming: (i) PBFM: 234 trained, 35% of which are women; (ii) General Management: 242 trained; 20% of which are women, and (iii) Gender Mainstreaming: 273, 47% of which are women.  

The lower percentage of women on the General Management courses reflected the low proportion of women in management positions at district level.  A post-training survey and evaluation was undertaken.  The Training and Development Decree 2017 requires districts to prepare annual and 5-Year training plans. 
Data Source: Governance and Public Administration Reform Program secretariat progress reports on the use of the District Development Fund; 
MOHA annual report</narrative>
    </description>
